{"entryId":"1552","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1552:1","sourceSha256":"18beba9ad332baeb881e6d057b395c85d0fc756469cf1b9810a7cc326b0eb2dc","englishSha256":"aabb72b667b335ff4105e156049de2e0f6a84ba4e3c48a87200b4f88f8c032a1","citations":[{"id":"1552:1:citation-01","he":[21,48],"en":[43,55],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_121b.16"},"reference":"Yevamot 121b:16","assessment":"The two direct versions distinguish a public report followed by remarriage from a version in which Rav Nachman permitted it. Preserve both attributed voices.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yevamot 121b:16","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_121b.16"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yevamot 121b:17","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_121b.17"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1552:1:citation-02","he":[181,226],"en":[286,312],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_57a.2"},"reference":"Bava Metzia 57a:2","assessment":"The received questions and answers are stated by the named transmitters here.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Metzia 57a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_57a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1552:1:citation-03","he":[272,308],"en":[422,495],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Bava_Metzia_57a.2.1"},"reference":"Tosafot on Bava Metzia 57a:2:1","assessment":"Tosafot directly calls Chasa Rav Nachman’s teacher. Preserve Heilprin’s explicit challenge separately.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tosafot on Bava Metzia 57a:2:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Bava_Metzia_57a.2.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1552:1:citation-04","he":[402,468],"en":[661,672],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_85b.4"},"reference":"Ketubot 85b:4","assessment":"The checked Bavli reads a silver cup (כסא דכספא), while the received Heilprin reads earthenware (